title: A Test of the Guardrails
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: not (dem_president = 1) and president == maga_leader and institutions < 70 and power_grab_done < 3 and month = 6 and power_grab_year != year
priority: 380
on-arrival: power_grab_year = year

= A Test of the Guardrails

The Republican administration is testing the limits of executive power: firing independent officials, defying judicial orders, and threatening critics. The guardrails of American democracy are being tested daily.

- @grab_courts: Fight in the courts
- @grab_streets: Fight in the streets and at the ballot box
- @grab_coalition: Build a bipartisan coalition for the rule of law
- @grab_wait: Wait for the next election

@grab_courts
on-arrival: power_grab_done += 1; institutions += 2; courts_independence += 2; maga_strength += 0.5; resources -= 0

Lawsuits pile up. Some win; some drag.

@grab_streets
on-arrival: power_grab_done += 1; civic_strength += 500; dem_enthusiasm += 1; polarization += 1; institutions += 1

Mass mobilization sends a warning.

@grab_coalition
on-arrival: power_grab_done += 1; gopmod_relation += 6; institutions += 3; pro_democracy += 2; progressive_dissent += 3

A handful of Republicans, business leaders, and judges join the effort.

@grab_wait
on-arrival: power_grab_done += 1; institutions -= 4; pro_democracy -= 2; subversion_progress += 0.5

We do not fight, and the guardrails weaken.
